// Branch 4: truth/validity separation (concept §6).

structure truth_validity_separated {
  ```
  Whether a mechanically verifiable fact holds is removed from human approval; humans judge only validity — whether the verification is appropriate evidence for the proposition
  ```
  children: verification_truth_by_machine, bind_validity_by_human, assumptions_surfaced
}

fiat verification_truth_by_machine {
  ```
  Verification outcomes are decided mechanically by veriq and CI; eval only reconciles the results and demands no human approval
  ```
  until: M8
  promote: bind
}

fiat bind_validity_by_human {
  ```
  The correspondence between a proposition and its verification (validity) is judged by a human within the local view, as a bind approval
  ```
}

fiat assumptions_surfaced {
  ```
  Every assumption a verification result relies on is aggregated mechanically through the interfaces and presented to the boundary bind approver as the total assumption set
  ```
  until: M8
  promote: bind
}
